    memcpy(pp->cache, pp->linestart_resp, pp->cache_size);
  ...
}
```

So `cache_size = clipamount = perline`. `perline` is the number of bytes in the current line. This can be up to `buffer_size` (1024). So `cache_size` max is 1024, not 1025.

Hmm. So `memcpy(ptr, pp->cache, pp->cache_size)` with `cache_size` up to 1024 writes at most 1024 bytes. If `ptr = buf`, that's within the 1024-byte buffer.

